# Pairs with EveryCommitEventuallyCovered. A silo falsely declared dead can
# commit after its declaration and stop before publishing; only the last
# re-invalidation of the false-death horizon covers that write. The mutant ends
# the horizon without it, so the write is never covered.
MODULE: HorizonClosesLeavesWriteUncovered
TARGET: EveryCommitEventuallyCovered
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the false-death horizon ends without re-invalidating the survivors
PERTURBS: HorizonCloses
BOUNDS: NumSilos = 1, MaxCrashes = 1, MaxFailures = 1, MaxFalseDeaths = 1

--- FIND
    /\ horizonOpen' = [horizonOpen EXCEPT ![s] = FALSE]
    /\ stale' = [u \in Silos |-> stale[u] \/ alive[u]]
    /\ scanDirty' = [u \in Silos |-> scanDirty[u] \/ (alive[u] /\ scanning[u])]
    /\ IF wstate = "crashed" /\ wsilo = s
          THEN /\ wstate' = "idle" /\ coveredVer' = regVer
          ELSE UNCHANGED <<wstate, coveredVer>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the horizon ends with no last re-invalidation.
    /\ horizonOpen' = [horizonOpen EXCEPT ![s] = FALSE]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<stale, scanDirty, wstate, coveredVer>>
--- END
